# Rust / Cargo build output
target/
**/target/

# Cargo.lock is not committed.
#
# Every Xmip module is a library, and a library's lock file is never read by
# anything that depends on it. More decisively: dependencies track `branch =
# "main"` under ADR-0005, and a committed lock pins a commit — which re-derives
# by hand exactly what tracking main exists to avoid, and churns in every
# module on every update.
#
# This is reversed at first release, when dependencies move from a branch to
# pinned versions and the assembly becomes something worth reproducing byte for
# byte.
Cargo.lock

